305-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20250305","date":"2025-03-05","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-04-14","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: The operation staff failed to ensure that all children were accounted for while transitioning the children out of the classroom to go into the gym at the end of the day, resulting in a child being left unattended in the classroom for approximately 15 minutes.  The operation terminated the caregiver responsible for the incident.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026629161","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20250305-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-707","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20250305","date":"2025-03-05","original_code":"746.707","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-04-14","finding":"Incident/Illness Report Form Shared with Parent: The incident report was not updated with the additional information that was viewed from the video after the self-report was made, which makes it unknown if the parents were told about the additional information.","topic":"health","source_record_id":"1026629159","violation_type_title":"Incident/Illness Report Form Shared with Parent (26 TAC §746.707)","topic_label":"Health records & medication"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20250305-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20250305","date":"2025-03-05","original_code":"746.2805(5)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-04-14","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Humiliating, Rejecting, Yelling: Based on the information gathered from interviews and video, a teacher was heard and seen on video using a yelling unpleasant type of tone and had an angry demeanor with the child that was left in the room unsupervised for 15 minutes.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026629163","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - Humiliating, Rejecting, Yelling (26 TAC §746.2805(5))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20241125","date":"2024-11-25","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":1,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905832606","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905832606","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-11-25","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20241125-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-613-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20241125","date":"2024-11-25","original_code":"746.613(b)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-12-05","finding":"Immunization Records, Exceptions, and Exemptions Current: One out of ten children's records was missing a current immunization.","topic":"health","source_record_id":"1026357205","violation_type_title":"Immunization Records, Exceptions, and Exemptions Current (26 TAC §746.613(b))","topic_label":"Health records & medication"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1332768-i20240806","date":"2024-08-06","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905832605","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y